                        "form": "функциона́лах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "588ece52-3725-3854-aa8d-438fa1b9fa21",
                        "entry_id": "b5dc4e06-87a5-386d-afee-86a13fcb65fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "матем. числовая функция, заданная на векторном пространстве"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1278ae68-40ed-4efa-afa6-15b43eff031e",
                                "sense_id": "588ece52-3725-3854-aa8d-438fa1b9fa21",
                                "text": "Функционал ― математическое понятие вариационного исчисления для обозначения переменной величины, заданной на множестве функций, т.е. зависящей от выбора одной или нескольких функций."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a867e531-1555-3615-9e1d-14214f918843",
                        "entry_id": "b5dc4e06-87a5-386d-afee-86a13fcb65fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "неол., комп. жарг. функция, которая имеет одну или несколько функций в качестве аргумента"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fedfde08-b8aa-3800-9181-df013ee143cf",
                        "entry_id": "b5dc4e06-87a5-386d-afee-86a13fcb65fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "неол., комп. жарг., собир. то же, что функциональность; набор функций, возможностей, предоставляемых компьютерной программой, библиотекой функций и т. п."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ceba7e4d-e5fc-4a12-bbc5-3f028ddc54c8",
                                "sense_id": "fedfde08-b8aa-3800-9181-df013ee143cf",
                                "text": "Первоначально эти системы создавались для предприятий, которые традиционно ведут производственную, финансовую, реже научную деятельность. В их базовом функционале отсутствуют модули, автоматизирующие основные виды деятельности вуза, связанные с образовательным процессом."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0765dd4e-0c50-358e-95f4-348dca6683b2",
                        "entry_id": "b5dc4e06-87a5-386d-afee-86a13fcb65fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "неол., жарг., собир. то же, что функциональность; перечень обязанностей, выполняемых работником"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "19c02209-ed81-45f3-881e-c67a321e335a",
                                "sense_id": "0765dd4e-0c50-358e-95f4-348dca6683b2",
                                "text": "Без принятия соответствующих поправок в Налоговый и Бюджетный кодексы главы местного самоуправления будут просто не в состоянии выполнять свой функционал."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "da73f9b8-018c-418c-9659-3c468cf793a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "b5dc4e06-87a5-386d-afee-86a13fcb65fc",
                        "source_sense_description": "математическое",
                        "target_lang_word": "functional",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "functional",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f64a7bc5-24a6-38aa-9fbc-84bf7e21618c",
                                        "entry_id": "8fc3ee6a-fb0f-3916-9731-8f48812acb51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In good working order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "636e90e7-5f2d-4223-861e-162c4f55413b",
                                                "sense_id": "f64a7bc5-24a6-38aa-9fbc-84bf7e21618c",
                                                "text": "While we assume that phonological subsyllabic units are functional prior to reading skill, we have not ruled out a possible interaction with the writing system."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abaf1fe4-1199-3974-bb7b-80a24a5b5918",
                                        "entry_id": "8fc3ee6a-fb0f-3916-9731-8f48812acb51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Useful; serving a purpose, fulfilling a function."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0759bd8c-d489-4daa-95fc-9a396d224699",
                                                "sense_id": "abaf1fe4-1199-3974-bb7b-80a24a5b5918",
                                                "text": "That sculpture is not merely artistic, but also functional: it can be used as a hatrack."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "073eb6e8-38b5-448c-8760-0b5fe1f335c8",
                                                "sense_id": "abaf1fe4-1199-3974-bb7b-80a24a5b5918",
                                                "text": "The two are often one and the same, says Walt Thompson, professor of kinesiology at Georgia State University and lead author of the ACSM survey – although functional fitness can apply to the younger generation as well."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6890c638-529a-33a5-ba58-b7c3b8a885d9",
                                        "entry_id": "8fc3ee6a-fb0f-3916-9731-8f48812acb51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Only for functional purposes, notably in architecture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3aeb5e88-dded-4896-a57e-69bcb409b6eb",
                                                "sense_id": "6890c638-529a-33a5-ba58-b7c3b8a885d9",
                                                "text": "A functional construction element generally must meet higher technical but lower aesthetical requirements."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfa47155-c875-3bdf-97d5-6ebdc5e93f22",
                                        "entry_id": "8fc3ee6a-fb0f-3916-9731-8f48812acb51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to one's role or office; official."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83c01831-9431-4038-9a32-f311791594ad",
                                                "sense_id": "cfa47155-c875-3bdf-97d5-6ebdc5e93f22",
                                                "text": "functional responsibilities"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd507e2d-a20e-32cb-99a6-1476726c4da8",
                                        "entry_id": "8fc3ee6a-fb0f-3916-9731-8f48812acb51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characterizing functioning in environment, being symptoms that do not presuppose alteration of organic structure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ca49aa7-20cf-4fd8-93fb-7ec244b5a03a",
                                                "sense_id": "dd507e2d-a20e-32cb-99a6-1476726c4da8",
                                                "text": "The clinical differentiation between functional and organic disease is at times difficult to establish, because, presumptively, in the beginning, at least, all organic disease is preceded by a physiologic perversion, that is, functional alteration, which may or may not be apparent with our present diagnostic limitations. […] Though benign rhythmic disturbances, such as premature contractions or paroxysmal tachycardia, do occur, it is notoriously difficult and still the subject of argument whether these may be called functionally benign or whether they may prove to have organic significance. […] The lack of opportunity for the medical student to observe the functional states in the medical school clinics and hospital practice, because of lack of space, or interest in their care in intramural teaching, is, I believe, a most forceful argument for a period of extramural practice under intelligent tutelage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53eb8267-23d2-4c82-8a10-cf55da208a0d",
                                                "sense_id": "dd507e2d-a20e-32cb-99a6-1476726c4da8",
                                                "text": "In our study of participants aged 18–39, increasing age was associated with improved functioning in laundry task and overall social functioning, encompassing prosocial activities, recreation, independence–competence, and employment. […] However, several longitudinal and cross-sectional studies indicate that these improvements tend to plateau by the late twenties, and may decline as individuals transition into middle adulthood (Clarke et al., 2021; Smith et al., 2012; Tomaszewski et al., 2025). These patterns suggest that while functional gains may be observed through early adulthood, they may not be maintained beyond the early thirties. Therefore, longitudinal studies extending into middle and late adulthood are critically needed to clarify how trajectories of activities of daily living and social functioning evolve throughout the lifespan."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46088646-7faa-3429-a579-3c8be5dedcc0",
                                        "entry_id": "8fc3ee6a-fb0f-3916-9731-8f48812acb51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to a function or functions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "184e4e32-e1e5-3df0-b8c0-3d051883a456",
                                        "entry_id": "8fc3ee6a-fb0f-3916-9731-8f48812acb51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having semantics defined purely in terms of mathematical functions, without side-effects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "functional",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8bca781b-17bf-38f0-aadd-0f942605549c",
                                        "entry_id": "cf438703-6026-30c2-b3ae-db0a9f750465",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A function that takes a function as its argument; more precisely, a function whose argument varies in a space of (real or complex valued) functions and whose value belongs to a monodimensional space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41ca76d2-54ed-4399-a9cc-34331447bd7b",
                                                "sense_id": "8bca781b-17bf-38f0-aadd-0f942605549c",
                                                "text": "An example of a functional is the definite integration of integrable real functions in a real interval."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0bbdfb00-bb23-3a6c-89a8-82c224e04b36",
                                        "entry_id": "cf438703-6026-30c2-b3ae-db0a9f750465",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A scalar-valued linear function on a vector space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d11eed7-b753-30dc-827b-e5d871bb0f8d",
                                        "entry_id": "cf438703-6026-30c2-b3ae-db0a9f750465",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An object encapsulating a function pointer (or equivalent)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
